Z||000000||theogre||11-13-2000||07:13 PM||||Recently there have been a few people who when they didn't get an instant answer opened another thread to ask people to look at their problem. One such post was placed 22 minutes after the first.<P>Please, Please, don't do that. <P>We'll get to you as soon as we can. This isn't a live support forum. There's not always someone here when you post. Odds are good you'll get an answer the same day. Often you'll get an answer in a couple hours. If you haven't gotten an answer yet it's usually because no one that has the answer has gotten on the system.<P>Posting more threads telling us to look at another thread isn't likely to get you an answer any sooner.<P>If you are in a real hurry try using the search function at the top of most pages. Chances are we've covered your problem before. Almost every post ever generated is on the system but may have been archived so don't forget to search there too.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||11-13-2000||07:19 PM||||If I may add to your post...<P>If your post gets far down on the page without any sufficient responses and your afraid it may get overlooked, simply repost to the same topic.  This will bring it back to the top without opening another thread.<P>||||reg||1
